 duration: "8 min",
 teacherNotes: "On screen or on On the whiteboard, write the common confusion below: '20% of S$50 ≠ 20% increase from S$50.' Explain: 20% of S$50 = S$50 ÷ 5 = S$10 (This isonepart, notincreaseafternewpricegrid). 20% increase from S$50: firstcalculate 20% of S$50 = S$10, againaddto S$50 → S$50 + S$10 = S$60 (thisonlyisnewpricegrid). writeoutcommonformula: Increase = original × percentage, New price = original + increase. Decrease samemanage: firstcalculate decrease amount, againsubtract. Have the child repeatscommonformula 2 times. ",
