 teacherNotes: "teachermodelfourcompleteexample questions (Write out reasoning steps), cover 4 kindmixcombineskillcan. example questions 1 (3.1 express as %, writing steps): Express 24 as a percentage of 80. Show your working steps. steps: ① A = 24, B = 80. ② (A ÷ B) × 100% = (24 ÷ 80) × 100%. ③ 24 ÷ 80 = 0.3. ④ 0.3 × 100 = 30. Answer: 30%. example questions 2 (3.4 increase, writing steps): Wei had S$60. His allowance was increased by 15%. What is Wei's new allowance after the increase? Show your working steps. steps: ① 15% of S$60 = 0.15 × 60 = 9. ② S$60 + S$9 = S$69. Answer: S$69. example questions 3 (3.5 reverse a decrease with discount story): Aisha bought a phone at a sale. After a 15% discount, the sale price is S$68. What was the original price before the discount? Show your working clearly. steps: ① After 15% discount, new price = original price × (1 − 15/100) = original price × 0.85. ② So S$68 = original price × 0.85. ③ Original price = S$68 ÷ 0.85 = S$80. Answer: S$80. example questions 4 (3.4 percentage point): The class attendance rate increased from 75% to 90%. (i) By how many percentage points did the rate increase? (ii) What is the relative percentage increase? steps: (i) 90% − 75% = 15 percentage points. Answer: 15 percentage points. (ii) Relative increase = (90 − 75) / 75 × 100% = 15 / 75 × 100% = 20%. Answer: 20% relative increase. Note: 15 percentage points ≠ 20% relative increase. Have the childcomprehensionthis 4 questionscover N3 3.1, 3.4, 3.5 threekindskillcan, atnotsameshouldusescenariomiddlemixcombinemakeuse. ",
