 teacherNotes: "teachermodelfourcompleteexample questions (Write out reasoning steps), cover 4 concept. example questions 1 (average rate): Wei reads 90 pages in 3 hours. What is his average reading rate? Show your working steps. steps: ① Total pages = 90. Total time = 3 hours. ② Average rate = total pages ÷ total time = 90 ÷ 3 = 30. Answer: 30 pages/h. example questions 2 (speed = distance ÷ time): Aisha cycles 18 km in 2 hours at constant speed. What is her speed? Show your working steps. steps: ① Distance = 18 km. Time = 2 hours. ② Speed = distance ÷ time = 18 ÷ 2 = 9. Answer: 9 km/h. example questions 3 (average speed, two-part journey): Wei cycles 60 km at 60 km/h, then 60 km at 30 km/h. What is his average speed for the whole journey? Show your working steps. steps: ① Part 1: distance = 60 km, speed = 60 km/h. Time = distance ÷ speed = 60 ÷ 60 = 1 hour. ② Part 2: distance = 60 km, speed = 30 km/h. Time = 60 ÷ 30 = 2 hours. ③ Total distance = 60 + 60 = 120 km. Total time = 1 + 2 = 3 hours. ④ Average speed = total distance ÷ total time = 120 ÷ 3 = 40. Answer: 40 km/h. (Note: The average of the two speeds (60+30)÷2 = 45 is WRONG. We must use total distance ÷ total time = 40 km/h.) example questions 4 (two-part with different distances): Mr Lim drives 40 km at 40 km/h, then 40 km at 20 km/h. What is his average speed? steps: ① Part 1: 40 km at 40 km/h. Time = 40 ÷ 40 = 1 h. ② Part 2: 40 km at 20 km/h. Time = 40 ÷ 20 = 2 h. ③ Total distance = 40 + 40 = 80 km. Total time = 1 + 2 = 3 h. ④ Average speed = 80 ÷ 3 = 26.67 km/h (round to 26.7 or keep as 80/3). For this week, use friendly numbers so answers are whole: 80 ÷ 3 ≈ 27 km/h (or state 26.67 km/h). Have the childcomprehensionfourquestionstotalsamepoint: average rate and speed allisuse total ÷ total (totalquantity ÷ totaltimebetween). Average speed nottwospeeddegreemean, onedetermineneedcalculateouteachsectiontimebetween, againuse total distance ÷ total time. ",
