 teacherNotes: "givechild 3 practice questions, Have the childdo independently, Write out reasoning steps. parent can use photo with phonechild reasoning. questions 1 (average rate): Wei prints 150 pages in 5 hours. What is the average printing rate in pages per hour? Show your working steps. answer: ① Total pages = 150. Total time = 5 hours. ② Average rate = total pages ÷ total time = 150 ÷ 5 = 30. Answer: 30 pages/h. questions 2 (constant speed): Aisha cycles from home to school, a distance of 18 km, at constant speed in 2 hours. What is her speed in km/h? Show your working steps. answer: ① Distance = 18 km. Time = 2 hours. ② Speed = distance ÷ time = 18 ÷ 2 = 9. Answer: 9 km/h. questions 3 (average speed, two-part journey with three sub-questions): Mr Lim drives from Riverside Secondary to Marina Bay. He drives the first 40 km at 40 km/h, then the next 40 km at 20 km/h. (i) What is the total distance? Show your working. (ii) What is the total time? Show your working clearly for each part of the journey. (iii) What is Mr Lim's average speed for the whole journey? Show your working. answer: (i) Total distance = 40 + 40 = 80 km. Answer: 80 km. (ii) Part 1: 40 km at 40 km/h. Time = 40 ÷ 40 = 1 h. Part 2: 40 km at 20 km/h. Time = 40 ÷ 20 = 2 h. Total time = 1 + 2 = 3 h. Answer: 3 h. (iii) Average speed = total distance ÷ total time = 80 ÷ 3 = 26.67 km/h (or 26.7 km/h, or 80/3 km/h). Answer: 26.67 km/h (not 30 km/h, which is the mean of 40 and 20). teachteacherpatrollookchild reasoning, correct format (If the child only writes answer, does not write steps, remind 'AEIS official exam requires working working steps'). If the childatquestions 3(iii)use (40 + 20) ÷ 2 = 30 km/h, point out: 'You took the mean of 40 km/h and 20 km/h and got 30 km/h. But that's WRONG for average speed! Look at the times: Mr Lim spent 1 hour at 40 km/h and 2 hours at 20 km/h. He spent more time at the slower speed. So the average speed must be closer to 20 than to 40. The correct way is: total distance ÷ total time = 80 ÷ 3 = 26.67 km/h. Average speed is NOT the mean of speeds.' If the childatquestions 3(ii)doesn't havedividesectioncalculatetimebetween, onlywrite total time = 3 h anddoesn't havewriteouteachsectiontimebetween, remind: 'Good! Your answer 3 h is correct. But the official requirement is to show your working clearly for each part of the journey. Please write: Part 1: 40 km at 40 km/h. Time = 40 ÷ 40 = 1 h. Part 2: 40 km at 20 km/h. Time = 40 ÷ 20 = 2 h. Total time = 1 + 2 = 3 h. This shows the method clearly.'",
