 teacherNotes: "On screen or on On the whiteboard, write the error example below: Wei draws a parallelogram with base 12 cm. The slanted side is 7 cm, and the perpendicular height from the base is 5 cm. Wei says: 'The area is 12 × 7 = 84 cm²' (mark as ✗). Ask the child: 「Is this correct? 'After the child thinks, circleerror: using the slanted side 7 cm as the height (error: useinclineslantedside 7 cm whenhigh). point out: Wei used the slanted side 7 cm as the height, but this is wrong (Wei useinclineslantedside 7 cm whenhigh, butThis iswrong). Why? Because the area of a parallelogram is base × perpendicular height, not base × slanted side (becauseflatlinefoursideshapeareaisbase × perpendicularstraighthigh, notbase × slantedside). The slanted side is NOT the height (inclineslantedsidenothigh). Write the corrections: Area = base × perpendicular height = 12 × 5 = 60 cm² (mark as ✓). Have the child repeat the corrected sentences: Area = 12 × 5 = 60 cm², not 12 × 7 = 84 cm². againgive Week two High-frequency errorexample: Aisha has a trapezium. The two parallel sides are 8 cm and 12 cm, and the perpendicular height is 5 cm. Aisha writes: 'Area = (8 + 12) × 5 = 100 cm²' (mark as ✗). Ask the child: 「Is this correct? 'After the child thinks, circleerror: forgetting the ½ in the trapezium formula (error: forgettrapezoidcommonformulamiddle ½). point out: Aisha forgot the ½. The correct formula is Area = ½ × (sum of parallel sides) × height = ½ × (8 + 12) × 5 = ½ × 20 × 5 = 50 cm², not 100 cm² (Aisha forget ½. correctcommonformulaisarea = ½ × (twoflatlineside) × high = ½ × (8 + 12) × 5 = 50 cm², not 100 cm²). Write the corrections: Area = ½ × (8 + 12) × 5 = 50 cm² (mark as ✓). Have the child repeat the corrected sentences: Trapezium area = ½ × (sum of parallel sides) × height. summarytwo High-frequency error: ① Parallelogram: don't use the slanted side as the height. Use the perpendicular height (flatlinefoursideshape: notneeduseslantedsidewhenhigh, needuseperpendicularstraighthigh). ② Trapezium: don't forget the ½ in the formula (trapezoid: notneedforgetcommonformulamiddle ½). ",
