 teacherNotes: "givechild 5 questions have the working on paper (Teacher does not give complete answer, only give prompts, Have the child writes out working steps): \n\npractice 1: Two cuboids form an L-shape. Cuboid A: 14 cm × 7 cm × 5 cm. Cuboid B: 10 cm × 7 cm × 4 cm. Joined along 7×4 face. Find the volume. (prompts: calculatetwo volume thenaddget up.) Expected answer: Volume A = 14×7×5 = 490 cm³. Volume B = 10×7×4 = 280 cm³. Total = 490 + 280 = 770 cm³.\n\npractice 2: A cuboid 15 cm × 12 cm × 10 cm has a cut-out 6 cm × 4 cm × 5 cm removed. Find the remaining volume. (prompts: large volume subtractsmall volume.) Expected answer: Large = 15×12×10 = 1800 cm³. Cut-out = 6×4×5 = 120 cm³. Remaining = 1800 - 120 = 1680 cm³.\n\npractice 3: A cylinder radius 7 cm and height 8 cm stands on a cuboid 24 cm × 14 cm × 6 cm. Find the total volume. Use π = 22/7. (prompts: cuboid volume + roundcolumn volume.) Expected answer: Cuboid = 24×14×6 = 2016 cm³. Cylinder = 22/7×7×7×8 = 22×7×8 = 1232 cm³. Total = 2016 + 1232 = 3248 cm³.\n\npractice 4: Two cuboids form an L-shape. Cuboid A: 10 cm × 6 cm × 4 cm. Cuboid B: 8 cm × 6 cm × 3 cm. Joined along 6×3 face. Find the surface area. (prompts: calculatetwo SA, thensubtractgo 2×(joined face).) Expected answer: SA of A = 2(10×6 + 10×4 + 6×4) = 2(60+40+24) = 2×124 = 248 cm². SA of B = 2(8×6 + 8×3 + 6×3) = 2(48+24+18) = 2×90 = 180 cm². Joined face = 6×3 = 18 cm². Total SA = 248 + 180 - 2×18 = 428 - 36 = 392 cm².\n\npractice 5: A cuboid 14 cm × 10 cm × 8 cm has a 5 cm × 4 cm rectangular hole cut 3 cm deep into one face. Find the new surface area. (prompts: originalcome SA subtractgodigfallsurface patch, addabove hole walls.) Expected answer: Original SA = 2(14×10 + 14×8 + 10×8) = 2(140+112+80) = 2×332 = 664 cm². Removed patch = 5×4 = 20 cm². Hole walls: 2(5×3) + 2(4×3) = 30 + 24 = 54 cm². New SA = 664 - 20 + 54 = 698 cm².\n\n If the child gets stuck, teachergivewordprompts (For example: 'use add stillis subtract? ' or 「joined face needsubtractseveraltimes? '), butnotstraightconnect Sayoutanswer. child calculatescompleteafter, teacher Check working steps and commonformula (volume: add or subtract; SA: subtract 2× joined face or add hole walls). ",
