 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 NUMBER AND ALGEBRA, N5. Algebraic manipulation: 5.14 factorisation of quadratic expressions ax²+bx+c (twotimesformulafactorformuladividesolve). This week is N5.14 only. Official method: For x²+bx+c, find two numbers that multiply to c and add to b, then write as (x+first)(x+second). Example: x²+5x+6 = (x+2)(x+3) (find 2 and 3: 2×3=6, 2+3=5). Signs: x²−5x+6 = (x−2)(x−3) (both negative: (−2)×(−3)=6, (−2)+(−3)=−5). Mixed: x²+x−6 = (x+3)(x−2) (one positive, one negative: 3×(−2)=−6, 3+(−2)=1). For 2x²+7x+3: test (2x+1)(x+3) = 2x² + 7x + 3 ✓. Friendly integers only. No calculator. Fossil: signs wrong ((x+2)(x+3) when it should be (x−2)(x−3)); or wrong factor pair ((x+6)(x+1) when it should be (x+2)(x+3), because 6+1=7 not 5). This week don't teach 5.15 multiplication and division of simple algebraic fractions (substitutenumberdivideformulamultiplication and division). this week, do not teach 5.13 grouping (Week 63 weekalready taught). this week, do not teach 5.12 identities (Week 62 weekalready taught). Cast: secondary Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary. Week 8–56 week completed Sec 1 content. Week 57 week completed Sec 2 N2.4 map scales. Week 58 week completed Sec 2 N2.5 direct and inverse proportion. Week 59 week completed Sec 2 N5.9 expansion of the product of algebraic expressions. Week 60 week completed Sec 2 N5.10 changing the subject of a formula. Week 61 week completed Sec 2 N5.11 finding the value of an unknown quantity in a given formula. Week 62 week completed Sec 2 N5.12 identities: (a+b)², (a−b)², a²−b². Week 63 week completed Sec 2 N5.13 factorisation of linear expressions ax+bx+kay+kby. this week, continue Sec 2 content (Sec 3 application preceding level). 'Tell the parent: 'this week High-frequency error focus: signs wrong (symbolerror, For example x²−5x+6 writebecome (x+2)(x+3) andnot (x−2)(x−3); expand (x+2)(x+3) = x² + 5x + 6, middleitemis +5x not −5x); or wrong factor pair (factornumbercorrecterror, For example x²+5x+6 writebecome (x+6)(x+1), but 6+1=7 notat 5, correctis (x+2)(x+3) because 2+3=5). correctdomethod: Find two numbers that multiply to c and add to b. Check both product AND sum. Write the factors, then expand to check. Signs: +5x → both +, −5x → both −, −6 (constant) → one + one −.'pleaseatparentendchecklookchildhomeworkraiseintersect, closenotethis High-frequency errorerror. 'correct, child Say: 'Great work today! Remember: Official 5.14 is quadratic factorisation. Find two numbers: multiply to c, add to b. Check the signs carefully. x²+5x+6 = (x+2)(x+3) ✓, x²−5x+6 = (x−2)(x−3) ✓. Always expand to check your answer.'Encouragechildandendlesson. ",
