 duration: "2 min",
 teacherNotes: "Welcome child. 'Today is Week 65 week AEIS secondary math, we learn Sec 2 N5.15 multiplication and division of simple algebraic fractions (substitutenumberdivideformulamultiplication and division). This week is N5.15 only, only teachofficialsubstitutenumberdivideformulamultiplication method and division method: monomial over monomial (oneitem Divided byoneitem), cancel common number and letter factors (eliminategocommonfactornumber and letter), leave the answer in simplest form (withmostsimpleshapeformulaworkanswer). official 5.15 wording (graduallywordleaduse): 'multiplication and division of simple algebraic fractions such as'. official such as example questions: (3a / 4b) × (5ab / 3); (3a / 4) ÷ (9a² / 10). This week don't teach 5.16 addition and subtraction of algebraic fractions with linear or quadratic denominators (substitutenumberdivideformulaaddition and subtraction, haslineproperty or twotimesdenominatorthatkind, thatis 5.16). this week, do not teach 5.14 factorisation of quadratic expressions (Week 64 weekalready taught). this week, do not teach 5.13 grouping (Week 63 weekalready taught). this week, do not teach 5.12 identities (Week 62 weekalready taught). Week 8–56 week Ialreadycomplete Sec 1 content, Week 57 week completed Sec 2 N2.4 map scales, Week 58 week completed Sec 2 N2.5 direct and inverse proportion, Week 59 week completed Sec 2 N5.9 expansion of the product of algebraic expressions, Week 60 week completed Sec 2 N5.10 changing the subject of a formula, Week 61 week completed Sec 2 N5.11 finding the value of an unknown quantity in a given formula, Week 62 week completed Sec 2 N5.12 identities: (a+b)², (a−b)², a²−b², Week 63 week completed Sec 2 N5.13 factorisation of linear expressions ax+bx+kay+kby, Week 64 week completed Sec 2 N5.14 factorisation of quadratic expressions ax²+bx+c, this week, continue Sec 2 content (Sec 3 application preceding level). 'tellchildthis week High-frequency error focus (High-frequency error): 「this week High-frequency error focus: forgetting to flip the second fraction when dividing (division methodtimeforget Week twodividenumberpourcome overagainmultiply: (3a/4)÷(9a²/10) errorcalculate (3a/4)×(9a²/10), shouldis (3a/4)×(10/9a²) ✓); or cancelling incorrectly (eliminategoerror, For example 3a and 9a² eliminatebecome 1 and 3, forgetdenominatorstillremainone a, correctshouldisnumerator 3a inside a and denominator 9a² insideone a eliminatefall, denominatorstillremain 3a). Icanoppositerepeatpracticethispoint, straighttochangefall. '",
