 teacherNotes: "Welcome child. 'Today is Week 68 week AEIS secondary math, we learn Sec 2 N6.7 graphs of quadratic functions and their properties (twotimesfunctionnumbergraph and itsproperties). This week is N6.7 only, only teachofficialthreeproperties: (1) positive or negative coefficient of x² (x² systemnumbercorrectnegative: when a > 0 the graph opens upwards and has a minimum point; when a < 0 the graph opens downwards and has a maximum point); (2) maximum and minimum points (mostlargepoint and mostsmallpoint: the turning point; for y = ax² + bx + c the axis of symmetry is x = −b/(2a), and the turning-point y-value is found by substituting that x into the function; friendly integers so −b/(2a) is an integer); (3) symmetry (correctcallproperty: the graph is symmetric about the vertical line x = −b/(2a)). This week don't teach 6.8 sketching graphs given in completed-square form or factorised form (don't teachfrommatchsquareshapeformula or factorformuladividesolveshapeformuladrawtwotimesfunctionnumbergraph). This week don't teach N7 equations (don't teachequation). Week 67 week completed N6.6 quadratic functions y = ax² + bx + c. this week, continue N6 Functions and graphs (functionnumber and graph), Learn 6.7 graphs of quadratic functions and their properties (twotimesfunctionnumbergraph and itsproperties). this week, continue Sec 2 content (Sec 3 application preceding level). 'tellchildthis week High-frequency error focus (High-frequency error): 「this week High-frequency error focus: sign error in −b/(2a) (at −b/(2a) middlesymboloutwrong: for y = x² − 4x + 3, writing axis x = −2 instead of x = 2); forgetting to substitute after finding the axis (findtocorrectaxis of symmetryafterforgetsubstitutefind y: stating turning point as (2, something wrong) because they didn't calculate y); saying 'opens upwards' and 「has a maximum' both true (Say'openoraltoabove' and 「hasmaximum'allcorrect, This iswrong: when a > 0, opens upwards means minimum, not maximum; when a < 0, opens downwards means maximum). '",
