 duration: "3 min",
 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 NUMBER AND ALGEBRA, N7. Equations and inequalities: 7.6 solving simple inequalities in the form ax + b ≤ c and ax + b < c and representing the solutions on the number line (solvesimplenotformula ax + b ≤ c and ax + b < c andatnumberaxisabove Representsolve). This week is N7.6 only. Official content: (1) isolate x in ax + b ≤ c and ax + b < c (friendly integers, no calculator). (2) if you multiply or divide both sides by a negative number, reverse the inequality sign (< becomes >, ≤ becomes ≥, > becomes <, ≥ becomes ≤). (3) represent the solution on the number line: closed circle for ≤ / ≥, open circle for < / >; shade/arrow the correct side. (4) distinguish < from ≤ on the number line (open vs closed circle). Friendly integers. No calculator. This week is N7.6 only: solve simple inequalities, reverse the sign when dividing by a negative number, represent on the number line with open or closed circle. This week don't teach 7.7 graphs (don't teachgraph). This week don't teach 7.8–7.10 simultaneous equations / quadratic equations (don't teachconnectstandequation, twotimesequation). This week don't teach G3 7.13 simultaneous inequalities (don't teachconnectstandnotformula). This week don't teach G2 / Sec-1-style 7.6 'ax ≤ b, ax ≥ b, ax < b, ax > b' (don't teach G2 version 7.6). (3) this week High-frequency error: forgetting to reverse the inequality sign when dividing by a negative number (Divided bynegativenumbertimeforgetchangenotsignsquareto); or confusing open circle (for < >) with closed circle (for ≤ ≥) on the number line (atnumberaxisaboveconfuseemptycenterroundpoint and actualcenterroundpoint); or putting the circle at the wrong value (roundpointdrawaterrorplaceplace). (4) remindchild: Week 70 weekhomeworkat app inside, belowweeksee. Cast: secondary Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary School. Friendly integers. No calculator.'",
