 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 NUMBER AND ALGEBRA, N7. Equations and inequalities: 7.8 solving simultaneous linear equations in two variables by: substitution and elimination methods, graphical method (solvetwodollaronetimesconnectstandequation: substitutemethod, eliminatedollarmethod, diagramsolvemethod). This week is N7.8 only. Official content: (1) a pair of linear equations in x and y; the solution is the pair (x, y) that satisfies both. (2) substitution: make one variable the subject of one equation, substitute into the other. (3) elimination: add or subtract equations after matching a coefficient. (4) graphical: each equation is a line; the solution is the intersection point. (5) check by substituting the solution back into both equations. Friendly integers only. No calculator. This week is N7.8 only: solving simultaneous linear equations in two variables by substitution (make one variable the subject, substitute into the other), elimination (add or subtract equations to cancel one variable), and graphical (each equation is a line; the solution is the intersection point). Check by substituting back into both equations. This week don't teach 7.9 quadratic equations by factorisation (don't teachfactorformuladividesolvesolveonedollartwotimesequation). This week don't teach 7.10 formulating a pair from a word questions as the main skill (not'fromshould use questionscolumnequationgroup'workasthis weekmainneedskillcan). (3) this week High-frequency error: offering both substitution and elimination as two correct options for the same pair on the same item (atsameone questionabove, sametimeraiseprovidesubstitutemethod and eliminatedollarmethodworkastwo「correct'option); or offering both 'the intersection is (a,b)' and 「x=a, y=b' as two keyed-correct options on one item (atsameone questionabove, sametimeraiseprovide'intersectpointis (a,b)' and 「x=a, y=b'workastwocorrectoption); writing pairs that copy BoardWeike examples (according tocopy BoardWeikeequationgroup); non-integer answers (answernotinteger); claiming a pair has two solutions (soundcallonecorrectnotsamestraight linehastwosolve). (4) remindchild: Week 72 weekhomeworkat app inside, belowweeksee. Cast: secondary Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary School. Friendly integers. No calculator.'",
