 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 NUMBER AND ALGEBRA, N7. Equations and inequalities: 7.9 quadratic equations in one variable by factorisation (factorformuladividesolvesolveonedollartwotimesequation). This week is N7.9 only. Official content: (1) a quadratic equation in the form ax² + bx + c = 0, where a ≠ 0. (2) solve by factorisation: rewrite the quadratic expression as a product of two factors, then set each factor to zero. (3) example: x² + 5x + 6 = 0 → (x + 2)(x + 3) = 0 → x = −2 or x = −3. (4) check by substituting each solution back into the original equation. (5) integer roots only (friendly integers, no calculator). This week is N7.9 only: quadratic equations in one variable by factorisation. Factorise ax² + bx + c = 0 into (x + p)(x + q) = 0, then set each factor to zero: x + p = 0 or x + q = 0. Check by substituting back. This week don't teach 7.10 formulating a pair of simultaneous linear equations from a word questions (don't teachfromshould use questionscolumnequationgroup). (3) this week High-frequency error: offering swapped factors (x − 4)(x − 3) vs (x − 3)(x − 4) as two correct options on the same item (atsameone questionabove, sametimeraiseprovidecorrectadjustafterfactorworkastwo'correct'option); offering both「x = 2 or x = 3'and'roots 2 and 3'as two keyed-correct options on one item (atsameone questionabove, sametimeraiseprovide「x = 2 or x = 3' and 'roots 2 and 3'workastwocorrectoption); keyed A that does not expand back to the given equation (option A factorformuladividesolveexpandafternotatquestionsdoequation); non-integer roots (answernotinteger); writing quadratics that copy the three BoardWeike example quadratics (x² + 5x + 6, x² − 3x − 10, x² − 4) (according tocopy BoardWeikeonedollartwotimesequation). (4) remindchild: Week 73 weekhomeworkat app inside, belowweeksee. Cast: secondary Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary School. Friendly integers. No calculator.'",
