 teacherNotes: "Welcome child. 'Today is Week 74 week AEIS secondary math, we learn Sec 2 N7.10 formulating a pair of linear equations in two variables to solve questions (fromshould use questionscolumntwodollaronetimesequationgroup). This week is N7.10 only, only teachfromshould use questionscolumntwodollaronetimesequationgroup: (1) read the word questions carefully, identify the two unknown quantities, and define variables (let x =... and y =...) clearly (carefulthinread Readshould use questions, recognized'ttwonotknowquantity, cleardeterminemeaningchangequantity x and y); (2) translate each condition in the questions into a linear equation in x and y (willaskquestionsmiddleeachitempieceturnchangeascloseat x and y linepropertyequation); (3) write the pair of equations together as a system (twoequationwriteatoneup, constructbecomeequationgroup); (4) the questions may then ask you to solve the system by substitution or elimination (askquestionsmaycancanneedfindyouusesubstitutemethod or eliminatedollarmethodfindsolve the equationgroup); (5) check your solution makes sense in the context of the questions (Checkyousolveataskquestionscontextmiddleisnocombinemanage); (6) integer coefficients and integer solutions only (friendly integers, no calculator) (only useintegersystemnumber and integersolve, friendgoodinteger, without calculator). this weekfocus: formulating the pair (columnequationgroup), not re-teaching elimination methods (notimportantnewteachsolve the equationgroupeliminatedollarmethod; Week 72 weekalready taught N7.8 solving). Week 72 week completed N7.8 solving simultaneous linear equations in two variables (solvetwodollaronetimesconnectstandequation). Week 73 week completed N7.9 quadratic equations in one variable by factorisation (factorformuladividesolvesolveonedollartwotimesequation). this week, continue N7 Equations and inequalities (equation and notformula), Learn 7.10 formulating a pair of linear equations in two variables to solve questions (fromshould use questionscolumntwodollaronetimesequationgroup). '",
