 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 NUMBER AND ALGEBRA, N7. Equations and inequalities: 7.10 formulating a pair of linear equations in two variables to solve questions (fromshould use questionscolumntwodollaronetimesequationgroup). This week is N7.10 only. Official content: (1) read the word questions carefully, identify the two unknown quantities, and define variables (let x =... and y =...) clearly; (2) translate each condition in the questions into a linear equation in x and y; (3) write the pair of equations together as a system; (4) the questions may then ask you to solve the system by substitution or elimination; (5) check your solution makes sense in the context of the questions; (6) integer coefficients and integer solutions only (friendly integers, no calculator). This week is N7.10 only: formulating a pair of linear equations in two variables to solve questions. Read the questions, identify the two unknowns, define x and y, identify the two conditions, translate each into an equation, write the pair, then (if asked) solve by substitution or elimination. Check your solution. this weekfocus: formulating the pair (columnequationgroup), not re-teaching elimination methods (notimportantnewteachsolve the equationgroupeliminatedollarmethod; Week 72 weekalready taught N7.8 solving). (3) this week High-frequency error: same pair in swapped order as two options; x/y swapped vs story (2x+y vs x+2y); one equation plus a dependent equation (sum/double); forming only one equation when story needs two; copying BoardWeike numbers in writing. (4) homework: app has 5 reading + 8 grammar + 3 writing. Reading and grammar are MCQ keyed A. Writing needs full working steps. Integer solutions only. No calculator. (5) This week we teach Learntool: BoardWeike whiteboardexample questions (on whiteboardthreecolumnequationgroupexample questions), helpyouremembercolumnequationgroupsteps. (6) Week 72 week completed N7.8 solving simultaneous linear equations in two variables (solvetwodollaronetimesconnectstandequation). Week 73 week completed N7.9 quadratic equations in one variable by factorisation (factorformuladividesolvesolveonedollartwotimesequation). this week Week 74 week, complete N7.10 formulating a pair of linear equations in two variables to solve questions (fromshould use questionscolumntwodollaronetimesequationgroup). belowweek, continuenewcontent. Singapore Teaching Practice: standardprepare Preparation (BoardWeike and whiteboardexample questions), model I do (teachermodel), bringpractice We do (teacherstudentoneupdo), independent You do (studentdo independently), Key questions and Af L format assessment, collectoralsummary. Readiness: recognized'ttwonotknowquantity, determinemeaningchangequantity. Engagement: trueactualcontext (stamps, stationery, class composition). Mastery: correctcolumnoutequationgroup, findsolve, test. Positive classroom culture: 'todayyou Learncanfromshould use questionscolumnequationgroup, This issolvedecideactualaskquestionsimportantneedskillcan. Keep practicing!'",
