 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 GEOMETRY AND MEASUREMENT, G2. Congruence and similarity: 2.1 congruent figures (congruent figure). This week is G2.1 only. Official content: (1) two figures are congruent if they have the same shape and the same size; (2) a rotation or reflection of a figure is still congruent to the original figure; (3) same shape but different size is NOT congruent, that is similar (next week G2.2); (4) same area does not mean congruent; (5) all corresponding sides and angles must be equal; (6) integer lengths and angles only, no calculator. This week is G2.1 only: congruent figures. Congruent = same shape AND same size. Rotation/reflection do NOT change congruence. Same shape different size = NOT congruent (that is similar, next week). Same area is NOT enough. (3) this week High-frequency error: same figure rotated/reflected offered as not congruent (wrong); same shape different size offered as congruent (wrong, that is similar); two options that are the same pair in different order; same area so congruent (wrong). (4) homework: app has 5 reading + 8 grammar + 3 writing. Reading and grammar are MCQ keyed A. Writing needs full explanation. Integer lengths and angles only. No calculator. (5) This week we teach Learntool: BoardWeike whiteboardexample questions (on whiteboardthreecongruent figureexample questions)+ Smath Figure diagramsolve (threediagram: twocongruentthreeangle (onerotateturn), twocongruentsquare (oneflipturn), twonotcongruentrectangleshape (Same shape, not samesize)), helpyouremembercongruentdeterminemeaning and characteristic. (6) Week 74 week completed N7.10 formulating a pair of linear equations in two variables to solve questions (fromshould use questionscolumntwodollaronetimesequationgroup). this week Week 75 week, complete G2.1 congruent figures (congruent figure). belowweek G2.2 Learn similar figures (similar figures). Singapore Teaching Practice: standardprepare Preparation (BoardWeike and whiteboardexample questions + diagramsolve), model I do (teachermodel), bringpractice We do (teacherstudentoneupdo), independent You do (studentdo independently), Key questions and Af L format assessment, collectoralsummary. Readiness: comprehensionsame shape and same sizeconcept. Engagement: trueactualfigure (triangles, squares, rectangles, circles), rotateturnflipturnchangechange. Mastery: correct Judgetwofigureisnocongruent, and solve it, explainingoriginalfactor. Positive classroom culture: 'todayyou Learncancongruent figuredeterminemeaning, knowrotateturn and flipturnnotchangecongruent. Keep practicing!'",
