 teacherNotes: "I do: Teacher on the whiteboardmodels oneexample questions (draw simple figures, markobjectbody, resemble, middlecenterpoint O, scale factor k). 'Problem: At Riverside Secondary, Mr Lim draws a triangle. Triangle DEF is enlarged by scale factor k = 2, centre O. DE = 4 cm, ∠D = 60°. Find image side D'E' and image angle ∠D'.」Step 1: Check k. k = 2 > 1, so enlargement (image bigger). Step 2: Image length = k × object length. D'E' = k × DE = 2 × 4 = 8 cm. Step 3: Angles do NOT change. ∠D' = ∠D = 60°. Answer: D'E' = 8 cm, ∠D' = 60°. teachteachersidemodelside Say: 「Notice: k = 2 > 1, so enlargement. D'E' = 8 cm > DE = 4 cm (image bigger). ∠D' = ∠D (angles unchanged). Draw centre O, object triangle DEF, image triangle D'E'F' (bigger, farther from O). All image vertices lie on lines from O through object vertices.'",
