 duration: "10 min",
 teacherNotes: "We do: Give child one question, and they work together todo (draw simple figures, markobjectbody, resemble, middlecenterpoint O, k). 'Problem: At Riverside Secondary, Aisha draws a square. Square ABCD is reduced by scale factor k = 1/3, centre O. AB = 9 cm, ∠A = 90°. Find image side A'B' and image angle ∠A'.」Have child say outeach step. teach Teacher guides: 「First, check k. Is k > 1 or 0 < k < 1?」(k = 1/3 < 1, so reduction.) 「Good. What does reduction mean?」(Image smaller.) 「Correct. What is the formula for image length?」(Image length = k × object length.) 「Yes. So A'B' = ?」(A'B' = k × AB = 1/3 × 9 = 3 cm.) 「Excellent. Check: 3 < 9, image smaller. ✓ What about ∠A'?'(Angles do not change, so ∠A' = ∠A = 90°.) 'Perfect. Answer: A'B' = 3 cm, ∠A' = 90°. Reduction (k = 1/3 < 1): image smaller. Angles unchanged.'",
