 teacherNotes: "Welcome child. 'Today is Week 86 week AEIS secondary math, we learn Sec 2 G4 trigonometric ratios of acute angles only (acuteanglethreeanglefunctionnumbercomparevalue). This week we teach sin θ = opposite / hypotenuse (sin θ = correctside / slantedside), cos θ = adjacent / hypotenuse (cos θ = adjacentside / slantedside), tan θ = opposite / adjacent (tan θ = correctside / adjacentside). Identify the ratio or find a missing side from a given ratio (recognizecomparevalue or according togivedeterminecomparevaluefindmissingside). Answers as integer lengths or unsimplified-OK integer fractions (answerkeepinteger or notsimplechangeintegerdividenumber, like 20/29). No calculator (without calculator). this weeknotfindangledegree (notuseoppositethreeanglefunctionnumber). This week don't teach 30-60-90 or 45-45-90 specialthreeangle (notdevelopclear √3 or √2). This week don't teach 3-D trig (don't teachthreedimensionemptybetweenthreeanglefunctionnumber). This week don't teach Pythagoras' theorem (threeanglealreadyisstraightanglethreeangle, sidealreadygivedetermine). Cast: Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary. Start the lesson. '",
