 teacherNotes: "summarythis weekfocus: (1) official Sec 2 AEIS math paper format: Part 1 MCQ 34 questions 30 min + Part 2 show working 20+10–15 questions 1 hour 45 min, without calculator. (2) this weekcontent: Sec 2 GEOMETRY AND MEASUREMENT, G4. Pythagoras' theorem and trigonometry: This week is trigonometric ratios of acute angles only (acuteanglethreeanglefunctionnumbercomparevalue). Official content: in a right-angled triangle, sin θ = opposite / hypotenuse, cos θ = adjacent / hypotenuse, tan θ = opposite / adjacent. Identify the ratio or find a missing side from a given ratio. Answers as integer lengths or unsimplified-OK integer fractions (e.g. 20/29). No calculator. this weeknotfindangledegree (do NOT find an angle in degrees, notuseoppositethreeanglefunctionnumber). This week don't teach 30-60-90 or 45-45-90 specialthreeangle (notdevelopclear √3 or √2). This week don't teach 3-D trig (don't teachthreedimensionemptybetweenthreeanglefunctionnumber). This week don't teach Pythagoras' theorem (threeanglealreadyisstraightanglethreeangle, sidealreadygivedetermine, don't teachfinishreachbrotherpull Sitheorem). (3) this week High-frequency error: swapping opposite and adjacent (correctside and adjacentsidedoopposite: sin = adj/hyp or cos = opp/hyp, correctis sin = opp/hyp, cos = adj/hyp); using tan when the question asks for sin (or vice versa) (questionsask sin butuse tan, or questionsask tan butuse sin, correctis Readclearquestions, sin and cos use hyp, tan use adj notuse hyp). (4) remember: sin = opp/hyp, cos = adj/hyp, tan = opp/adj. Mnemonic: SOH CAH TOA. Opposite is the side opposite to the angle. Adjacent is the side next to the angle, not the hypotenuse. Hypotenuse is the longest side, opposite the right angle. sin and cos use hypotenuse. tan uses adjacent, not hypotenuse. Check: sin and cos are always < 1. tan can be > 1 or < 1. lookthis week homework entry (/learn pagesurface Week 86 week), docomplete it and the system will auto-grade, Iat We Chat groupinsidesamestepadvancedegree. '",
